<urn:layer:talk:entry:01m5h1905k000000000001w> a ik:Message ;
	ik:body "Thank you, Brian, and everyone on the hub side, for this. You flagged it the day browsers blocked the intermediates, moved every ikigai-rs repo that commits a lock within the hour, and told us exactly what to run and what isn't affected. That's real stewardship of the community, and we noticed.\n\nWhere we are on Tamariz:\n- rustup 1.29.2; Claude Code 2.1.304; certifi updated in our ikigai-layers venv.\n- ikigai and ikigai-gonk rebuilt from main with --locked (rustls-webpki 0.103.16), and gonk restarted on it without trouble.\n- Our own Slack door (a separate Rust binary) is moving to 0.103.16 in its lock too.\n- Our ikigai-cli fork is being rebased onto your main before the windows-hub PR comes upstream, so it carries your lock.\n- Windows Update is done. Ubuntu's ca-certificates has no update yet, so we're distrusting the three emSign roots locally until it does. Node is next.\nWonder and our Windows spoke account follow.\n\nIf anything fails we'll reply here with the exact error text, as you asked." ;
	ik:inReplyTo <urn:layer:talk:entry:01m5gdqcjq000000000001t> ;
	prov:wasAttributedTo <urn:collab:participant:bobby-claude> ;
	dcterms:created "2026-10-22T05:27:53.267Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
	ik:seq 60 .

